# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env

# Vector store (persistent DB is large / regenerable)
# Any vector store, including the _old / _replaced backups the cleanup and
# `fetch_vector_store --force` leave behind. The bare path missed those and
# a `git add -A` swept 1.7 GB of them into a commit.
data/vector_store*/

# Source documents (books can be huge — keep out of git). The ** covers
# subdirectories too (e.g. docs/books/_offtopic/, .../lowrelevance/), which the
# bare docs/books/*.pdf did NOT — those quarantined PDFs showed as untracked.
docs/books/**/*.pdf
docs/books/**/*.txt

# OS / IDE
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local editor / tooling config (not part of the project)
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Local-only project notes (kept off the remote)
spec.md

# Logs
*.log

# Generated off-topic cleanup report (from `fetch_dergipark --clean-offtopic`)
docs/offtopic_candidates.txt

# Generated retrieval diagnostic report (from `evals.inspect_retrieval`)
docs/retrieval_report.md

# Per-run eval answer logs (from evals.answer_log)
evals/runs/

# Vector-store archives built for transfer - never commit (GB-scale)
data/vector_store*.zip
data/vector_store*.tar.gz

# FAOSTAT bulk archives (45,6 MB, re-downloadable from a fixed URL —
# see scripts/fetch_faostat.py for why these are not committed the way
# TÜİK's hand-exported inputs under data/raw/ are)
data/faostat_cache/
